## 2026-11-18 — Premium P30 complete
- Hover, magnifier, zoom, and pan motion per premium §8.4, §8.5. A discrete wheel now springs (`spring-camera`) to `exp(−deltaY × 0.0015)` about the cursor, and consecutive notches compound on the running target. A `ctrlKey` trackpad pinch stays 1:1. Release inertia is a real decay (× 0.998 per ms, stops below 0.02 px/ms); an out-of-bounds end, and the pinch release past [1, 8] or the pan bounds, return on `spring-throw`. The drag rubber-band uses b = stage half-size. Drag pans only at zoom > 1. Double-click zooms 2.5× at scale 1, otherwise fits. Under reduced motion the wheel jumps and a drag or pinch clamps to the bounds with no rubber-band and no inertia. The magnifier hides while any gesture, spring, or inertia moves the camera (`setCameraMotion`), returns only after the next pointer move, and hides with opacity only over `dur-1` (scale resets to 0.96 once hidden, so a re-entry reverses from the current opacity).
- Verified: typecheck and lint clean, `pnpm test` 347/347 (54 files; 8 new camera tests). After a fresh build, the new e2e `zoom-pan-p30` passes 3/3, as do `magnifier-p23` (A10), `wafer-stage-r6` (now waits for the wheel spring to settle), `perf-gate` (0 frames > 50 ms, median 16.7 ms, p95 33.2 ms), `stage-controls-p10`, `evidence-ignite-p29`, `overlay-states-p8`, and `coach-marks-p25`. `linked-interactions-r7` failed only its known 780 ms settle step (821 ms). No snapshot changes, no locale keys.
- Decisions (restrained): the pan bounds stay as they were. Read literally, "disc centre must stay inside the stage" would stop edge dies being reached at zoom > 2 and would break the evidence framing. The current bounds already keep the disc centre inside the stage at scale 1 and keep the stage centre on the disc when zoomed. A `ctrlKey` wheel pinch clamps to [1, 8], because it has no release event to spring back from. Scale above 8 also rubber-bands during a touch pinch, as before.
